# Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io/). GitLab does
# not render a "Cite this repository" panel the way GitHub does, but the format
# is forge-independent: cffconvert, Zenodo and the R package cffr all read it,
# which is why it still ships. Kept out of the CRAN tarball via .Rbuildignore.
# After you replace the maintainer identity, add your ORCID below, and once the
# package has a Zenodo DOI add `doi:` and an `identifiers:` block.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "seor"
# TODO(ORCID): add `orcid:` under authors once an ORCID iD is registered.
abstract: >-
  The 'seor' suite bundles a set of focused R packages for search engine optimization and web-developer workflows: URL parsing, punycode and internationalized-domain conversion, public suffix list lookups, XML sitemap parsing and PageRank estimation. Loading 'seor' with a single call to library() installs and attaches all of the member packages at once, in the style of the 'tidyverse' metapackage.
version: 0.0.0.9000
authors:
  - family-names: Turczynski
    given-names: Bart
    email: bartek@turczynski.pl
repository-code: "https://gitlab.com/bart-turczynski/seor"
url: "https://seor-272402.gitlab.io"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - R
  - rstats
  - CRAN
  - seo
  - metapackage
